# owned by sys-apps/horcrux-repo-config: USE changes the Horcrux role packages need (read while Portage resolves the role package, so they cannot ship with it)
# Podman networking (netavark) builds nftables rules through the json interface
net-firewall/nftables json
# lxc (tools,caps) links libcap statically
sys-libs/libcap static-libs
# incus clustering (dqlite/raft)
dev-libs/raft lz4
dev-util/xdelta lzma
# the manager (app-emulation/horcrux-bin) and every Horcrux VM console need QEMU with SPICE (lab finding 2026-11-05: QEMU "-spice: invalid option" on every laptop).
# Here and not in horcrux-bin: Portage reads this while it resolves horcrux-bin's own dependencies, a file horcrux-bin installs would come too late.
app-emulation/qemu spice usbredir virtfs vnc zstd
# the Horcrux Console encoder (an ffmpeg child process): H.264 (x264) and VP8 (libvpx)
media-video/ffmpeg vpx x264
# ffmpeg (Console encoder) pulls media-libs/harfbuzz (drawtext/libass); harfbuzz's default `cairo` USE (hb-view/hb-shape tools only) dragged x11-libs/cairo into a
# headless server's world update (daily server-systemd red 2026-11-20). Nothing on a Horcrux host needs harfbuzz's cairo tools.
media-libs/harfbuzz -cairo
